  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The spelling and the Aramaic and Arabic parallels identify the night word independently of its position under לטש “sharpen” in the index. SEDRA lexeme 1675 gives the Syriac noun. Isaiah 34:14 names a creature, לִילִית, for which Akkadian lilītu (Oracc armep/x000101240) is a separate lexical comparison. Its derivation from the Hebrew word for night is uncertain."
